# AppDock news
[page]
title=AppDock 8 - What's new (Page 1)
text=Please report bugs, feature requests, etc. via GitHub Issue or DChat. Thanks for your support.
image=assets/logos/appdock.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=Digital Independence
text=Dchat 2.0.0: The DM server is now hosted by supabase. No more Manus shit.
image=assets/logos/network.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=New Homescreen
text=Closer to android, re-arrangeable apps, App logos
image=assets/lockscreen/appdock_lockscreen_hero.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=Recent apps
text=Steve Jobs once introdued the home button: "It takes you home wherever you are". Swipe up from the lower screen edge, no matter where you are. A dock with recent apps opens.
image=assets/logos/display.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=Keys - Simple control
text=Click the page turn key (Multi: Upper one) to incerase brightness. Long-press it for power options. Multi: Lower key long press -> Screensaver animation
image=assets/logos/appdock_logo.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=DuckDuckGo and AppDock Store
text=The home screen gained a DuckDuckGo search bar. The AppStore became a Google Play-style AppDock Store with a catalog, installation flow, and app details. The store header, scrolling, and search refresh were subsequently improved.
image=assets/logos/app_store.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=Visual layout editor
text=The home screen can be edited visually. Apps and widgets can be arranged and moved in the layout, and a more discoverable entry point opens the editor. A pinned-item move crash was fixed and layout changes are stored persistently.
image=assets/logos/appdock.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=The GOOGLE age
text=REAL YouTube and YouTube Music were introduced.
image=assets/logos/settings.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=App redesign
text=To improve the visual power of AppDock, some Apps like FM or Settings were redesigned to look like Android Apps
image=assets/logos/file_manager.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=Window Manager - Computer Mode
text=Beta Feature: Launch DApps as movable, resizeable Windows, explore multitasking and more.
image=assets/logos/display.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.8.9–7.8.11 · YouTube foundation and E-Ink video
text=The YouTube DApp downloads videos with yt-dlp and ffmpeg, converts them to the E-Ink-compatible BWR format, and provides a local library and player. Conversion gained fast scaling, larger bounded batches, optimized BWR2 processing, and reusable framebuffers. The player catches up more efficiently after seeks.
image=assets/logos/web_browser.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.8.12–7.8.23 · YouTube tools and reliable downloads
text=YouTube gained automatic tool setup, visible live shell output, ARMv7 and legacy-libc support, safe runtime extraction, bounded compatibility checks, and useful bootstrap errors. Downloads use the Android YouTube client and protect against hanging or incomplete processes.
image=assets/logos/web_browser.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.8.24–7.8.31 · YouTube audio, BWR2, and sync
text=Video and companion WAV audio are generated and played together. BWR2 compression, audio/video synchronization, DASH fragment downloads, batched frame reads, cached monow detection, and faster ffmpeg conversion were added. GStreamer clock handling, fallbacks, and timing corrections were repeatedly stabilized for Kobo devices.
image=assets/logos/music.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.8.32–7.8.43 · Configurable video offset
text=The video start offset after audio begins can be set from immediate playback to 60 seconds, including decimal values. Multiple audio backends are supported. Variable source offsets, leading silence, MTK latency, audio clocks, and real-time playback were corrected; the stable real-time clock replaced the unreliable frame lock.
image=assets/logos/music.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.8.42–7.8.51 · YouTube Watch view and library
text=YouTube uses the same Watch-oriented structure in portrait and landscape, with a main video, Up next rail, search, actions, and navigation. The library is clickable, uses safe thumbnails or the first BWR frame, can delete videos with their WAV and old thumbnails by long press, and shows proportional, undistorted previews. An inline mini-player and smoother E-Ink rendering were added.
image=assets/logos/web_browser.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.0–7.9.2 · Draw and color video
text=The Draw DApp provides a pen, eraser, brush sizes, line, rectangle, circle, fill, layers, undo/redo, saving and loading of bounded .adraw projects, and JPEG export through an existing ffmpeg. YouTube can optionally create BRC2 color videos using white, black, red, green, and blue. AppDock-owned dialogs and the Draw tile were introduced, and a Draw startup rendering issue was fixed.
image=assets/logos/document.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.3–7.9.9 · Stability, dithering, and fullscreen
text=Dialog tap geometry, page-key holds, rotation, Draw geometry, and color devices were stabilized. BRC2 color processing gained YUV color selection, multi-color error diffusion, and later precomputed dither patterns; frame expansion became much faster. YouTube gained true fullscreen, better audio pipelines, and smoother playback. Dialogs and Draw toolbars became more readable.
image=assets/logos/display.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.10–7.9.14 · Draw expansion and YouTube Music
text=Color videos mix multiple allowed palette colors with fast, precomputed dithering. Audio stops reliably when leaving the app. The BWR2 decoder reduces peak memory through direct delta, RLE, and zlib processing. YouTube Music downloads audio only, creates WAV files, shows full-color covers, and provides a library, search, and player. Draw gained a classic toolbar, shapes, live preview, gesture-based fill, partial refresh, and undo/redo.
image=assets/logos/music.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.15–7.9.20 · Music, Draw color, and windows
text=YouTube Music keeps partial results visible, exposes search errors, supports searching with Enter, and has an improved player with artist, cover, duration, and controls. Draw supports RGB color selection, color displays, RGB32 output, and correct brush sizes. The beta window mode gained a taskbar, start menu, multiple movable and resizable windows, minimize, restore, individual close, and fullscreen.
image=assets/logos/music.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.21–7.9.27 · Stylus support
text=Draw supports Kobo stylus pressure, eraser, marker, rotation, and KOReader's public stylus callback. Separate strokes, lift slots, pressure fallbacks, device-specific pressure_event codes, and pressure curves are handled correctly. Fast stylus samples are processed immediately; refreshes are reduced without losing samples, and only the final refresh blocks synchronously.
image=assets/logos/document.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.28–7.9.29 · Lock screen and Music layout
text=The lock screen was redesigned in an Android-inspired style with clock, date, profile card, initials, pattern points, PIN, and swipe action. The existing AppDock lock still protects AppDock only. YouTube Music Like, Saved, and More action chips were centered and protected against overflow on different display widths.
image=assets/lockscreen/appdock_lockscreen_hero.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.30 · Safe downloads and readable themes
text=Theme palettes choose contrasting text colors. Store wallpapers are validated before activation. YouTube jobs check inputs, write permissions, processes, and empty sources; BWR output is written temporarily and installed atomically only after success. DuckDuckGo renders safe Instant Answer links. Sort my files scans each folder once, skips symlinks, and preserves paths. AI Chat Agent and Geometry Dash received local updates.
image=assets/logos/settings.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.32–7.9.40 · Search, themes, and Bluetooth
text=Search gained a DuckDuckGo HTML fallback. The multi-page update dialog reads editable content from features.adf. Store theme images are resolved relatively and stored in binary form; DApp colors are resolved for contrast. Volume is persistent. Bluetooth moved from imported code to AppDock's own bluetoothctl control and then to Kobo/BlueZ D-Bus support for MTK and standard BlueZ.
image=assets/logos/network.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.34–7.9.39 · Update dialog and background jobs
text=The update dialog appears after startup, detects new versions reliably, and is separate from the setup wizard. The wizard remains available manually in Settings. If features.adf is missing, a safe single-page fallback is shown. DApp background checks run in subprocesses without blocking the UI and are stopped when the plugin closes. Lockscreen profile images can be selected with the native file chooser.
image=assets/logos/dockupdate.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.41–7.9.48 · Faster keyboard
text=The keyboard gained Cancel, larger keys, CAPS for persistent uppercase, correct German characters, and three local completions. An editable TSV database contains 3,000 German and 3,000 English words with frequencies. Lazy loading, safe plugin paths, multiple database paths, and a small fallback list prevent boot crashes while reliably loading the complete database.
image=assets/logos/appdock.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.49 · Reliable startup and clear control
text=The update dialog appears on every start until Don't show again is selected, uses a stable light modal card, and shows a test image without a timeout. The boot protection stores the last working plugin version locally and restores it after a boot crash. Sort my files recognizes Documents, Images, Videos, Audio, Apps, and Folders virtually and persistently without moving files. Store DApps receive contrast-checked text roles.
image=assets/logos/dockupdate.png
buttons=Next

[page]
title=7.9.49 · Faster YouTube conversion
text=Video and audio conversion run serially for stability, but use two decode threads, one filter thread, and four frames per pipe read. Only one conversion job runs per device. The video UI processes up to 128 frames per tick with a maximum CPU window of 0.30 seconds. Pipes, writers, temporary files, and background processes are closed safely on errors.
image=assets/logos/web_browser.png
buttons=Done
